  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte and Touche obligated $495M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Deloitte and Touche received 165 awards, with an average award size of $3M, and obligations are down 26.1% year over year. Department of Defense is the largest buyer for Deloitte and Touche with $200M in obligations, followed by Department of Health and Human Services with $95.6M and Department of Veterans Affairs with $50.1M. Other Computer Related Services is the largest market for Deloitte and Touche at $384M, followed by Other Accounting Services at $79.2M and Offices of Certified Public Accountants at $17.3M. Deloitte and Touche also records obligations in Custom Computer Programming Services at $9.4M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $9.2M, with smaller activity in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $719K. Current-year totals are partial because the period covers FY2026 to date, so the profile focuses on where Deloitte and Touche is contracting now and which markets and agencies account for the largest shares of obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers of Deloitte and Touche?",
        "body": "Department of Defense obligated $200M from Deloitte and Touche, making the Department of Defense the largest buying agency. Department of Health and Human Services obligated $95.6M, and Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $50.1M. Department of Homeland Security obligated $36.6M and Department of the Treasury obligated $30.8M, rounding out the next tier of buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets drive Deloitte and Touche's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services accounts for $384M of Deloitte and Touche obligations and is the largest market. Other Accounting Services accounts for $79.2M and Offices of Certified Public Accountants accounts for $17.3M. Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $9.4M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $9.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
